# Logging (Slf4j)

Use Lombok `@Slf4j` on services, listeners, mail handlers, filters/handlers that already do.

## Levels

| Level | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `info` | Business milestones (create/update/delete/login success, mail send start) |
| `debug` | Noisy reads (paging, “still valid token”) |
| `warn` | Expected degradation (bad login, Redis down fail-open, mail send failed but flow continues) |
| `error` | Failures that need attention (OAuth failure, unhandled exceptions, mail MessagingException in MailService) |

Prefer parameterized messages: `log.info("Creating article with title: {}", title)`.

## Never log

- Passwords, raw JWT / refresh tokens, `Authorization` headers
- Mail SMTP credentials, OAuth client secrets
- Full request bodies that may contain secrets

Log **usernames, emails, entity ids, titles** — not secrets.

## Controllers

Do not add logging in controllers; log in services / listeners.
